pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% The RUP half of the coefficient-tier coverage, and the one the shipped corpus
% otherwise leaves untested: a propagation whose slack arithmetic runs entirely
% above i64. `2^64 x1 >= 2^64` propagates x1 (slack without x1 is 0, far below
% the degree) and the unit `~x1 >= 1` then conflicts, so `rup >= 1` derives the
% contradiction and the formula really is unsatisfiable.
%
% The kernel's NARROW instantiation cannot hold 2^64 and stands down; the bridge
% replays the same certificate at the unbounded instantiation, where slackTerms
% and slackWithout are exact. That is the arithmetic the wrapped-watcher-slack
% wrong verdict (defect 10) lived in at the i128 tier, so this instance exists
% to keep the wide RUP path from going dead: if it ever stops being replayed,
% tests/kernel_verify_expected.txt gains a skip and drops the composed verdict.
% Do not "simplify" the coefficient: the instance is worthless below 2^63.
f 2;
rup >= 1 ;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT : 3 ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
